{
  "analysis": "We are at /app with no prior commands run. Need inspect the video file and available tools, then extract/analyze frames to identify the Zork moves typed by the player and write them to /app/solution.txt.",
  "plan": "Run basic inspection commands: list /app, probe video metadata, and check for ffmpeg/ffprobe/python/OCR tools. This will determine how to extract frames and transcribe the gameplay text.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /app\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which ffmpeg ffprobe python3 tesseract convert montage 2>/dev/null || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ffprobe -v error -show_entries format=duration:stream=width,height,r_frame_rate,nb_frames -of default=noprint_wrappers=1 /app/video.mp4\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The video exists at /app/video.mp4. Only python3 is available from the common media/OCR tools; ffmpeg/ffprobe/tesseract/ImageMagick are missing. We need inspect which Python libraries are installed for video frame extraction and image processing.",
  "plan": "Check for Python modules such as cv2 (OpenCV), PIL/Pillow, numpy, av, imageio, and moviepy. Also check OS package availability as a fallback. If a video library is present, we can extract frames and analyze them programmatically.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - <<'PY'\nmods = ['cv2','PIL','numpy','av','imageio','moviepy','decord','skimage','pytesseract','easyocr']\nfor m in mods:\n    try:\n        __import__(m)\n        print(m, 'OK')\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(m, 'NO', type(e).__name__, str(e)[:80])\nPY\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport struct, sys\np='/app/video.mp4'\nwith open(p,'rb') as f:\n    data=f.read(32)\nprint(data[:8], data[16:20], data[20:24])\nPY\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get --version 2>/dev/null | head -1 || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The video is a Matroska/WebM file. No Python media/OCR libraries are installed, and ffmpeg/ffprobe are absent. apt is available, so the next step is to try installing ffmpeg (and ideally ImageMagick/tesseract) for frame extraction and OCR. If package installation works, we can extract frames and analyze the Zork terminal text.",
  "plan": "Run apt-get update, then install ffmpeg and tesseract-ocr/ImageMagick. After installation, probe video metadata and extract sample frames to inspect resolution/content. If apt has no network, we will fall back to parsing with Python libraries or other installed tools.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get update\n",
      "duration": 10.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y ffmpeg imagemagick tesseract-ocr\n",
      "duration": 20.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The package installation is in progress and downloading/installing many dependencies. We need to wait for it to finish before proceeding with ffmpeg/OCR tools.",
  "plan": "Wait for the apt-get install command to complete, then verify ffmpeg/ffprobe/tesseract are installed and probe the video metadata.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "",
      "duration": 30.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The apt install failed due to transient network errors fetching a few packages. Many packages were downloaded successfully, so retrying with --fix-missing may complete the installation. If it still fails, we can try installing only ffmpeg with fewer dependencies.",
  "plan": "Retry apt-get install with --fix-missing to fetch the failed packages and complete installation. Then verify the installed tools and probe the video.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y --fix-missing ffmpeg imagemagick tesseract-ocr\n",
      "duration": 30.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The apt retry still failed on libapparmor1, so ffmpeg/tesseract may not be installed yet. We should check whether any partial install left usable binaries and inspect dependency alternatives. If ffmpeg is still missing, try a narrower no-recommends install or retry with retries, since the failure appears transient/package-specific.",
  "plan": "Check for ffmpeg/ffprobe/tesseract binaries and dpkg status. Also inspect which package pulls in libapparmor1 and whether a minimal ffmpeg-only install can avoid it. Then attempt a no-recommends install of ffmpeg only if needed.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which ffmpeg ffprobe tesseract convert 2>/dev/null || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "dpkg -l | grep -E 'ffmpeg|tesseract|imagemagick|libavcodec|libavformat' || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-cache depends ffmpeg | head -80\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-cache rdepends libapparmor1 | head -40\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends ffmpeg\n",
      "duration": 30.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The no-recommends ffmpeg installation is progressing and setting up packages. We need to wait for completion, then verify ffmpeg is available and probe the video.",
  "plan": "Wait for the current apt-get install to finish. Then run verification commands for ffmpeg/ffprobe and probe the video metadata.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "",
      "duration": 30.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which ffmpeg ffprobe || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
