    {
      "keystrokes": "ffprobe -v error -show_entries format=duration:stream=width,height,r_frame_rate,nb_frames,codec_name -of default=noprint_wrappers=1 /app/video.mp4\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "ffmpeg/ffprobe are now installed. The video is 1280x720, 30 fps, 190.1 seconds long, H264 video with Opus audio. We need extract frames and read the Zork terminal text to identify player moves. Tesseract may not be installed yet, so we should try installing it and also extract sample frames to inspect the content.",
  "plan": "Create a frames directory, extract sample frames at 5-second intervals for initial inspection, and attempt to install tesseract-ocr separately. Then we can OCR frames or analyze them visually to identify each command typed.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /app/frames && ffmpeg -hide_banner -loglevel error -y -i /app/video.mp4 -vf \"fps=1/5\" /app/frames/sample_%03d.png\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends tesseract-ocr\n",
      "duration": 20.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /app/frames | head -50\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which tesseract || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "ffmpeg extracted 38 sample frames at 5-second intervals from the 190s video. Tesseract is still not installed, so OCR is not yet available. We need install OCR tooling or otherwise inspect/convert frames. The next step is to retry installing tesseract and verify it.",
  "plan": "Retry installing tesseract-ocr with no recommends. Then verify the binary is available and run a quick OCR test on one sample frame to see if the terminal text is readable.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends tesseract-ocr\n",
      "duration": 20.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which tesseract || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tesseract /app/frames/sample_001.png stdout --psm 6 2>/dev/null | head -80\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Tesseract is now installed and OCR works on the extracted frames. The first frame shows Zork I starting at West of House with score 0, moves 0. We need OCR all sample frames or extract more frequent frames to track the game text and identify each command the player types. The sample at 5s intervals may miss fast typing, so first let's OCR all current samples to see the progression, then refine extraction as needed.",
  "plan": "Run Tesseract on all current sample frames and save the text to /app/ocr_samples.txt for review. Then display the OCR text with frame markers to understand the game progression and identify commands.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "for f in /app/frames/sample_*.png; do echo \"=== $(basename \"$f\") ===\"; tesseract \"$f\" stdout --psm 6 2>/dev/null; echo; done > /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The OCR loop may still be running; no output has appeared yet because the loop redirects to a file, and the subsequent cat may be waiting or has not executed until the loop finishes. We need wait/poll for completion, then inspect the generated OCR text.",
  "plan": "Wait a few seconds for the Tesseract loop and cat command to finish, then display the OCR samples file with line numbers if needed.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l /app/ocr_samples.txt; sed -n '1,220p' /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The previous commands appear to still be in progress or the terminal output is not yet refreshed. The Tesseract OCR loop over 38 frames may take more than a few seconds. We need wait for it to finish and then inspect the file.",
  "plan": "Wait longer for the OCR loop and subsequent commands to complete, then check the output file and terminal state.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -l /app/ocr_samples.txt; wc -l /app/ocr_samples.txt; sed -n '1,240p' /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The terminal is echoing queued commands but not showing results, which indicates the OCR loop is still running and blocking subsequent commands. Tesseract on 38 frames can take some time. We need wait for the loop to finish.",
  "plan": "Wait longer for the OCR loop to complete, then inspect the output file once the shell prompt returns.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "\n",
      "duration": 30.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -l /app/ocr_samples.txt; wc -l /app/ocr_samples.txt; sed -n '1,260p' /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The OCR loop has completed and the terminal is showing part of the output. I can see some Zork gameplay text including commands like 'e', 'w', 'put solid', 'case', 'n', 'push all'. I need inspect the full OCR output systematically to identify all player moves and their order.",
  "plan": "Display the full OCR samples file with line numbers and frame markers. Then use that to reconstruct the sequence of player commands. If 5-second samples miss commands, extract frames more frequently or focus on prompt lines.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n '^=== ' /app/ocr_samples.txt; echo '---'; cat -n /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "We have OCR from 5-second sample frames. The tail shows the game reaches a winning state with 262 moves, so we need reconstruct the full command list, not just the sampled commands. I need inspect the full OCR text and then extract frames more densely around changes to capture all prompt lines/commands.",
  "plan": "Print the full OCR samples in manageable chunks with line numbers, and grep for prompt-like lines (lines containing '>' or ending with cursor markers). This will reveal what commands were captured at 5s intervals and where sampling missed commands.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,300p' /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '301,600p' /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '601,900p' /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '901,1200p' /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n -E '^>|>$|>.*_$|^[a-z].*_$' /app/ocr_samples.txt | head -200\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The 5-second OCR samples give a rough outline and show the game ends with 262 moves, but they are too sparse to capture every command. I need inspect the full sampled OCR text and then use frame change detection/cropping to capture all prompt lines. First, let's view the OCR text in chunks and get bounding box info from Tesseract to locate the input prompt region.",
  "plan": "Print /app/ocr_samples.txt in smaller chunks to understand the whole sampled progression. Then run Tesseract TSV on a sample frame to find the vertical coordinates of the bottom prompt/input line, so we can crop and OCR that line from many frames efficiently.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,200p' /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '201,400p' /app/ocr_samples.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
